# makepkg's working files. The PKGBUILD and its companions are tracked;
# nothing makepkg produces is.
#
# scripts/linux/build.sh --packages exports SRCDEST/BUILDDIR/PKGDEST so none
# of this lands here in the first place — build/ and dist/ are ignored
# wholesale at the repo root, which is a far stronger guarantee than the
# patterns below. These exist for the case where makepkg is run BY HAND from
# this directory, where its defaults put everything in $startdir, i.e. right
# here.
#
# A `git+https://` source makes makepkg keep a BARE CLONE of the whole
# repository next to the PKGBUILD, named after the source (whisper_player) —
# tens of MB that has no business being committed. See Matrix_Player's
# packaging/arch/README.md for the incident this pattern is copied from.
whisper_player/
src/
pkg/
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.pkg.tar.zst.sig
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
